# kendex-guard-dialect: legacy-glob
# Markdown exclusions use pattern<TAB>reason. Globs match full repository paths;
# * crosses /. A ! entry includes matching files again. Read by md-format,
# md-refs, prose, and md-reflow. Two classes only: bytes this repository does not
# author, and bytes a reformatting would damage. Everything VGS writes is held to the format.
backend/vendor/*	vendored Go modules for offline builds; the tree must match upstream exactly or vendor verification fails
!backend/vendor/AGENTS.md	VGS-authored instructions for the vendored tree, held to the format
config/vshell/nvim/colorschemes/*	vendored upstream colourscheme plugins, carried verbatim
!config/vshell/nvim/colorschemes/AGENTS.md	VGS-authored instructions for the vendored tree, held to the format
!config/vshell/nvim/colorschemes/ATTRIBUTION.md	VGS-authored: maps each vendored plugin to its upstream and licence, maintained here
quickshell/vshell/assets/sounds/plasma/*	vendored upstream sound theme, carried verbatim
quickshell/vshell/LICENSE_CHANGE_12_11_2025.md	licence notice; reflowing legal text would alter a document meant to stay verbatim
.agents/*	kendex render output, owned upstream; a local reflow is erased by the next refresh
!.agents/skills/vgs-distro-publish/*	VGS-owned in-place skill, declared source = "in-place" in kendex.toml
!.agents/skills/vgs-release/*	VGS-owned in-place skill, declared source = "in-place" in kendex.toml
!.agents/skills/vshell-dev/*	VGS-owned in-place skill, declared source = "in-place" in kendex.toml
.claude/*	kendex render output, owned upstream
.codex/*	kendex render output, owned upstream
.opencode/*	kendex render output, owned upstream
.pi/*	kendex render output, owned upstream
.cursor/*	kendex render output, owned upstream
